From: Jonathan Barnes <hello@jonbarnes.dev>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 17:00:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] The dust collides with a body instead of being blown by it

Patch 0042 of the renderer series (OoT: Recompiled).

The user, 2026-10-08, the first time a figure's push actually reached the dust: "The interaction
with link is not smooth and it feels very choppy and it also feels like it's pushing way past where
his body is ... rotating them around his body almost ... Can we just have normal collision? It
doesn't have to cause wind gusts or anything like that. Maybe just have it cause collision and then
it'll just roll off".

A mover in the light list is now a body where it stands this frame: the game's own collision
cylinder, its foot at the position, its radius in the attenuation radius and its height in the point
radius (the program carries it forward between the game's updates). A mote that would be inside the
body, taken as a capsule so it has no corner, sits on its skin instead, the nearest way out, and
slides round it as the body passes. 0037's carry, spill, lift and widening wake and 0039's sweep are
gone, and a body reaches no further than its skin plus BodySkin, so the movers near a ray are found
by that reach too.

diff --git a/src/shaders/Raytracing.hlsl b/src/shaders/Raytracing.hlsl
--- a/src/shaders/Raytracing.hlsl
+++ b/src/shaders/Raytracing.hlsl
@@ -1477,60 +1477,42 @@ static const float DustFaintest = 0.12f;      // patch 0038: the faintest mote's
 static const float DustBrightnessSpread = 0.35f;   // patch 0038: how far a mote's brightness lies from the row's, either way
 static const float DustDrift = 0.3f;          // how far a mote wanders from its place, as a share of its cell
 
-// THE THINGS THAT MOVE THROUGH THE DUST (patch 0037, the user, 2026-10-08: "as Link runs through
-// it ... the dust would be moving along with Link in that direction, like it would be pushed, and
-// then air would kind of flow out behind Link and ... bellow out"; "all things that can receive a
-// shadow or cast a shadow should also interact with the dust"). The program hands over a trail of
-// samples of every actor that moved, in the light list with this group bit (no light, only a
-// position, the motion in world units a second, a reach, and the age in seconds), and every light
-// loop passes them over. A mote near a young sample is carried along with the motion; as the
-// sample ages its wake widens, and the air spills outward from the path and lifts a little, then
-// settles as the sample dies, so a figure running through dust pushes it ahead and leaves it
-// billowing behind. (AirMoverBit itself is declared beside the beams' bit, before the passes
-// that pass over it.)
-static const float MoverLife = 1.0f;          // seconds a trail sample pushes for
-static const float MoverSpreadRate = 1.5f;    // how much wider a wake grows each second, as a share of the reach
-// A REAL PUSH (patch 0039, the user, 2026-10-08: "link is passing right through the particles
-// rather than him interacting with them"). 0037's push was a gentle carry held under half a cell,
-// so a figure thirty units across walked straight through. Now the newest samples' bodies sweep the
-// air clear: a mote inside MoverBody of a fresh sample is pushed out to its edge. The carry, the
-// spill and the lift are stronger, and the march finds a pushed mote by looking it up through the
-// push (dustInLight), so a push may reach well past the mote's own cell.
-static const float MoverBody = 32.0f;         // world units round a mover's middle that its body sweeps clear
-static const float MoverFresh = 0.2f;         // seconds a sample counts as where the body still is
-static const float MoverCarry = 0.18f;        // seconds of the motion a mote at the heart of the push is carried
-static const float MoverSpill = 0.1f;         // how far out the air spills behind, per unit a second of the motion
-static const float MoverLift = 0.05f;         // how far up it billows, the same way
-static const float MoverTopSpeed = 400.0f;    // world units a second; anything faster pushes as hard as this
-
-float moverSpread(PointLight light) {
-    return light.attenuationRadius * (1.0f + light.flickerIntensity * MoverSpreadRate);
+// THE THINGS THAT MOVE THROUGH THE DUST COLLIDE WITH IT (patch 0042). Patches 0037 and 0039 made
+// a moving actor an air current: a trail of samples a tenth of a second apart, each carrying the
+// motes along, spilling them outward and lifting them as it aged. It never reached the dust until a
+// reader fix in the program, and when it did the user found it wrong: "not smooth and it feels very
+// choppy and it also feels like it's pushing way past where his body is ... rotating them around his
+// body almost ... Can we just have normal collision? It doesn't have to cause wind gusts or anything
+// like that. Maybe just have it cause collision and then it'll just roll off" (2026-10-08).
+//
+// So each sample is now a BODY where it stands this frame: the game's own collision cylinder, its
+// foot at the position, its radius in the attenuation radius and its height in the point radius,
+// carried forward by the program between the game's twenty updates a second so it moves smoothly.
+// A mote that would be inside a body sits on its skin instead, the nearest way out, and slides
+// round it as the body passes; once the body has gone by the mote is where it always was. Nothing
+// is carried, spun or lifted, and nothing past the skin moves. The body is a capsule, the cylinder
+// with its ends rounded, so a mote meets no corner to jump across.
+// (AirMoverBit itself is declared beside the beams' bit, before the passes that pass over it.)
+static const float BodySkin = 3.0f;           // world units outside the cylinder that still count as touching
+
+float bodyReach(PointLight body) {
+    return body.attenuationRadius + BodySkin;
 }
 
-float3 moverPush(float3 mote, PointLight light) {
-    const float age = light.flickerIntensity;
-    const float life = saturate(1.0f - age / MoverLife);
-    if (life <= 0.0f) {
+float3 moverPush(float3 mote, PointLight body) {
+    const float radius = bodyReach(body);
+    const float bottom = body.position.y;
+    const float low = bottom + radius;
+    const float high = max(bottom + body.pointRadius - radius, low);
+    const float3 nearest = float3(body.position.x, clamp(mote.y, low, high), body.position.z);
+    const float3 r = mote - nearest;
+    const float distance = length(r);
+    if (distance >= radius) {
         return float3(0.0f, 0.0f, 0.0f);
     }
 
-    const float3 r = mote - light.position;
-    const float distance = length(r);
-    const float3 away = (distance > 1.0e-3f) ? (r / distance) : float3(0.0f, 1.0f, 0.0f);
-    const float fresh = saturate(1.0f - age / MoverFresh);
-    const float clear = max(MoverBody - distance, 0.0f) * fresh;
-
-    const float spread = moverSpread(light);
-    const float weight = exp(-(distance * distance) / (spread * spread)) * life * life;
-    const float3 velocity = light.direction;
-    const float rawSpeed = length(velocity);
-    const float speed = min(rawSpeed, MoverTopSpeed);
-    const float3 carried = (rawSpeed > 1.0e-3f) ? (velocity * (speed / rawSpeed)) : float3(0.0f, 0.0f, 0.0f);
-    const float3 side = float3(r.x, 0.0f, r.z);
-    const float sideLength = length(side);
-    const float3 outward = (sideLength > 1.0e-3f) ? (side / sideLength) : float3(0.0f, 0.0f, 0.0f);
-    const float passed = saturate(age * 4.0f);   // the spill and the lift come once the mover has gone by
-    return away * clear + weight * (carried * MoverCarry + outward * (speed * MoverSpill * passed) + float3(0.0f, speed * MoverLift * passed, 0.0f));
+    const float3 skinward = (distance > 1.0e-3f) ? (r / distance) : float3(1.0f, 0.0f, 0.0f);
+    return skinward * (radius - distance);
 }
 
 uint4 dustHash(uint4 v) {
@@ -1650,7 +1632,7 @@ float3 dustInLight(float3 origin, float3 direction, float end, uint2 launchIndex
     const uint steps = min(uint(range / stepLength) + 1u, DustMaxSteps);
     const float pixelAngle = RtParams.fovRadians / max(RtParams.viewport.w, 1.0f);
 
-    // The movers whose wake reaches this ray at all (patch 0037).
+    // The bodies that could reach this ray's motes at all (patch 0037; 0042: a body's whole capsule).
     uint movers[DustMaxMovers];
     uint moverCount = 0;
     const uint lightCount = min(RtParams.lightsCount, RtParams.maxLights);
@@ -1660,9 +1642,13 @@ float3 dustInLight(float3 origin, float3 direction, float end, uint2 launchIndex
             continue;
         }
 
-        const float reach = moverSpread(mover) * 2.5f;
-        const float closest = clamp(dot(mover.position - origin, direction), 0.0f, range);
-        if (length(mover.position - (origin + direction * closest)) < reach) {
+        // Measured from the capsule's middle, not its foot (the position): a ray past a figure's
+        // chest is further from its feet than its radius, and the first build of 0042 picked
+        // nobody that way. The reach is the whole capsule and a cell, for a mote pushed in.
+        const float3 middle = mover.position + float3(0.0f, mover.pointRadius * 0.5f, 0.0f);
+        const float reach = bodyReach(mover) + mover.pointRadius * 0.5f + DustCell;
+        const float closest = clamp(dot(middle - origin, direction), 0.0f, range);
+        if (length(middle - (origin + direction * closest)) < reach) {
             movers[moverCount] = m;
             moverCount++;
         }
